    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenDevelopersHelp">Developer studio names included in the description template.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenEstimatedLengthHelp">Approximate playtime when it can be inferred from available context. Left empty when there is no reliable estimate.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenFeaturesHelp">Main feature list for the description (usually rendered as a bullet list).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenFeature1Help">First item from the generated feature list (same as {feature_1}).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenFeature2Help">Second item from the generated feature list (same as {feature_2}).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenFeatureNHelp">Inserts one feature by index from the features list. Replace N with 1, 2, 3â€¦ Extra tokens stay empty if fewer features were generated.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenGameplayHelp">How the game plays: main loop, systems, controls feel and what the player actually does.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenGenresHelp">Genre names generated for the description template.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenNotesHelp">Extra editorial notes that do not fit the other description fields.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenPerspectiveHelp">Camera or view style (first person, third person, isometric, side-scrolling, top-down, etc.).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenPlayModesHelp">Known play modes such as single-player, local/online co-op, competitive multiplayer or campaign.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenPremiseHelp">Core narrative premise or high-level concept of the game, without full plot spoilers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenPublishersHelp">Publisher or company names included in the description template.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenRecommendedForHelp">Who the game is for (player taste or audience). Not hardware requirements â€” use {recommended_sys_req} for those.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenRegionsHelp">Regions associated with the game when relevant to the description.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenSettingHelp">World, place or setting where the game takes place (era, planet, city, fantasy realm, etc.).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenShortHelp">Short editorial summary of what the game is. Usually one or a few sentences. Length can be overridden in Advanced.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenSimilarGamesHelp">Free-text block about comparable games. For individual names in a list, prefer {similar_game_N}.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenSimilarGame1Help">First similar game name from the generated list (same as {similar_game_1}).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenSimilarGame2Help">Second similar game name from the generated list (same as {similar_game_2}).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenSimilarGameNHelp">Inserts one similar game name by index. Replace N with 1, 2, 3â€¦ Extra tokens stay empty if fewer names were generated.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenSynopsisHelp">Longer synopsis covering premise, context and structure. Can span several paragraphs depending on the Synopsis length setting.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenTagsHelp">Tag names generated for the description template.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="MTDA_TokenMinSysReqHelp">Minimum PC system requirements copied from Steam store data. Not invented by the AI. Empty when Steam has no data or the game cannot be matched.</sys:String>
